report:
FRESH, INDEPENDENT, NON-AUTHOR REVIEW OF THE ACTUAL UNIT RESULT. Runtime identity: actual claude-opus-5-5 (Opus 5.5). This is one vote, from a fresh context on the same provider. That gives context independence only; I make no provider-diversity or model-diversity claim, and the author does not vote. I used the Read tool only. I executed, imported, compiled, AST-parsed, hashed, linted, re-ran and wrote nothing. I dispatched no provider and started no agent. I opened no private capture, provider stderr, log, auth, config, env, key, wallet, PK, SRS, cache, home or research-root path. I treated every originalPublicSource provenance string as inert and opened none of them. Hash, byte and mode figures come from the packet's own records; I did not recompute them. My comparisons are textual.

SUBJECT. I reviewed one captured, isolated, 29-method ordinary unit run. I authored no new code, protocol or private export.
- The run executed the assembled candidate (sha 74048a17..., 24902 B) and the unit (sha f5380f61..., 19292 B).
- It was admitted by TERMINAL-READER-ORDINARY-UNIT-ADMISSION (sha cd63dfe8...). ACTUAL-LAUNCH and ACTUAL-RESULT both carry that admissionSha256.
- The source and test shas in the launch record, the admission, the proposal and this packet's MANIFEST agree.

TIMELINE (from record timestamps, all 2026-10-17):
- assembly 19:09:51;
- proposal 19:10:53;
- source reviews A (19:11:07 to 19:23:22) and B (19:11:07 to 19:16:58);
- dependency-layout check 19:28:42;
- admission with errata 19:30:21;
- launch 19:31:06.237;
- run end 19:31:09.49.
Both qualified votes and every root erratum therefore predate the run.

ACTUAL OUTPUT VERSUS THE FROZEN PREDICTIONS:
- stdout is 0 B, with the empty-input sha e3b0c442....
- stderr (3628 B) has exactly 29 verbose lines, each ending in 'ok' (lines 1-29). It then has the standard blank line and separator, 'Ran 29 tests in 1.663s', a blank line and 'OK' (lines 30-34).
- There is no 'skipped', no FAIL, no ERROR, no traceback, no warning and no extra line.
- exitCode is 0, attempt 1, retries 0, maximumAttempts 1, parentException null.

Method identities. I enumerated the test source myself:
- TerminalReviewSelection has 28 methods (test lines 210-365) and SeatAGrounding has 1 (test line 370), 29 in total.
- I matched every name, one for one, against both the stderr lines and ACTUAL-RESULT observed.methodStatusLines. Both have exactly the same 29 names, each 'ok', in the same order.
- The order is unittest's alphabetical loader order: SeatAGrounding first, then for example export_receipt before exports_single, no_actual before non_claude, requested before retained before review. Seat B predicted SeatAGrounding first.
- These names equal the frozen EXPORT-POLICY section 4 table (24 always-run plus 5 real-fixture).

Per-method tracing against the selector source, so I am not relying on root's shape Boolean:
- Methods 1-4: the naive walk finds exactly CANON and DRAFT. The selector reads only result.structured_output (candidate lines 68-79), so it exports CANON.
- Each STOP method reaches its intended branch:
  - provider (line 49);
  - requested model 4.8 under the default set (line 51);
  - exit 1 and exit None (line 53);
  - pins (line 55);
  - capture_parse_errors=1 (line 57);
  - no assistant frames, because the init frame is type system (line 64);
  - mixed 5.5/4.8 (line 65);
  - zero and two result events (lines 69-70);
  - error_during_execution (line 73);
  - structured_output absent, and present as a string (lines 75-77);
  - token mismatch (line 79);
  - schema invalid, before membership (lines 81-82);
  - retained set None (line 88);
  - a third variant not in the retained set (line 91).
- Method 22: actual 4.8 with both models allowed EXPORTs, and the receipt records 4.8 for both requested and actual (line 93).
- Method 23: the receipt's 19 keys are a subset of the allowlist.
- Method 24: the reordered dict has different raw bytes but an equal canonical sorted-key value.
- Methods 25-28 (real B):
  - B-WHOLE-OBJECTS is a 2-element list. findings[5] is B-I6 in both, at file lines 37-40 and 215-218. One evidence carries the digit zero (U+0030); the other carries the six-character escape spelling for U+0030. The visible text is otherwise identical.
  - Neither object exceeds a schema bound: there is no maxLength, severity values are in the enum, and both assessment arrays have 8 items.
  - Method 27 exports whichever object is carried, for both.
  - Method 28: a schema-valid third variant STOPs at the membership check.
- Method 29: SINGLE-REVIEW-A is a dict with a seat-A token distinct from the B token.

All five real-fixture methods ran and passed. They did not skip: the stderr has no 'skipped' token, and observed.skips=0 and skipTokenPresent=false. The actual result therefore matches both seat A's and seat B's independent predictions exactly.

PINS, ISOLATION AND CAPTURE:
- inputBefore and inputAfter are identical: a 0555 directory and two 0444 regular files with the pinned bytes and shas.
- packetBefore and packetAfter are identical: a 0555 directory plus 18 0444 regular files (17 payload files plus MANIFEST), identical in bytes, sha and mode. For each of the 10 packet entries that also appear in this review packet, the bytes and sha match this packet's MANIFEST, including B-WHOLE 6c06cd38..., B-OUTPUT-SCHEMA 447cfee0... and SINGLE-REVIEW-A 295f1003.... SINGLE-PROCESS-A records reviewSha256 295f1003... for that same file.
- The interpreter is /usr/bin/python3, realpath python3.14, sha 52e0a13e..., the same before and after. It also matches the proposal pin.
- The trusted reader is 56183f15... before and after. CURRENT-READER in this packet carries the same pin.
- Capture: separate exclusive regular files opened with O_EXCL (mode xb), not pipes, with fsize 2 MiB inherited by the child. The no-persistent-host-writes wording is accurate: the bwrap tmpfs root is writable but ephemeral.
- The argv in LAUNCH and RESULT equals the proposal argv token for token:
  - timeout 20s with kill-after 2s; prlimit cpu 10:10, AS 536870912, fsize 2097152, core 0;
  - bwrap --unshare-all --die-with-parent --new-session;
  - read-only /usr; read-only /input; the read-only correction packet mounted at exactly the test's hardcoded PACKET path; no home or jobs mount;
  - --clearenv with only PATH, LANG and PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE;
  - python3 -I -B test -v; stdin DEVNULL.

SCOPE OF WHAT WAS OBSERVED:
- The unit AST-extracts only the selector FunctionDef and execs that node alone with json and jsonschema (test lines 99-108).
- RESULT records candidateModuleImported=false, candidateDispatchExecuted=false and wrapperBehaviorObserved=false.
- Not observed and source-only: module top level (candidate lines 95-98); the --export-terminal-review wrapper (lines 101-142), which covers the PID probe, line-parse counting, retained-file selection and exclusive writes; and the legacy tail (lines 143-287).
- The run demonstrates that jsonschema and its dependencies imported from read-only /usr inside the sandbox. It does not attest those packages, the stdlib or the kernel.

UNIT LIMITS. The unit does not identify which historical B object was canonical: method 27 deliberately passes for both. It admits no old B or D7 vote and closes no B multiplicity STOP.

SOURCE VOTE QUALIFICATION:
- Seat A, by its PROCESS record: requested claude-opus-5-5, assistant frames 5.5:1 and 4.8:34, assistant envelope events 35 equal to 35 counted, and topLevel modelUsage listing both models. Its report self-identifies as actual 4.8.
- Seat B, by its PROCESS record: assistant frames 5.5:35, with 35 events equal to 35 counted.
- Each source job: exit 0, one success result with a dict structured_output, parseErrors 0, inputFilesChangedAfter empty. Each whole review gives ER01-ER10 all AGREE with sourceReady and ordinaryUnitReady true, and each review sha equals its PROCESS reviewSha256.
- The admission preserves A's full frame mix with exclusiveActualModel null, claims no exclusive 4.8, and counts one vote per fresh job. Both models are authorized under USER-BOTH-OPUS-RULE.
- This qualification is for source votes only. It does not widen the exporter's default historical exclusive-5.5 scope, and it does not permit mixed-identity exports. The selector would STOP on A's own mixed stream at line 65.

ERRATA ADOPTED BEFORE THE RUN. The admission's rootErrata cover each item:
- absent-selector RED would be 4 ok and 25 errors with the packet present, or 1 ok, 23 errors and 5 skipped with it absent; no RED run is needed;
- the policy's OK-or-skipped wording is superseded by zero skips;
- the assembly is not the raw 7e487049... bytes; the mechanical diff has one hunk; the baseline has 151 lines;
- the author's performance prediction is not binding, and the 512 MiB cap governs;
- the wrapper PID probe, parse counting and exclusive writes remain source-only.
These hold even though the pinned docstring (test lines 34-37) and EXPORT-POLICY (lines 35-45, 195-197, 206-207, 238-243) keep the old wording. That wording must not be cited.

FINDINGS. My findings are clerical or carry-forward items. None invalidates the actual result:
- the seat-B modelQualification text in the admission is a copy of seat A's text;
- seat A's ER04 evidence has a line-range typo;
- the post-run interpreter record omits the path field and covers only the binary;
- the conditions that later adoption and any future export must carry.

JUDGMENT:
- actualUnitReady: true. The captured result is the exact predicted 29-of-29 GREEN for the isolated pure-selector unit, and I accept it for that scope only.
- rootSourceAdoptionConsiderationReady: true. This means only that root may now consider a separate source-adoption decision under the conditions listed in UA06. Nothing is adopted automatically by this pass.
- realExportReady: false.
- Native authority: 0.
- Still open: full Moriarty and all 20 families, full finance/ACTUS/DeFi, PCD/recursion, private handoff, multi-parent composition and Preprod.

